Compile out Kimchi's self-update: Nix owns the binary, and the store copy is
read-only. Every update gate is hardwired off: the launch path returns before
probing, the shared workflow finds no update for `kimchi update`, `/update`
stops before its menu (so no toggle and no "enable auto-update" tip), and the
tip rotation drops the auto-update tip. Each gate is a one-line condition, so
the patch touches no import block or help text; `/update` keeps upstream's
notice wording. The `opts.signal!` assertion keeps TypeScript's narrowing in
the now-unreachable launch path.

